As I smell the sweet scent of approaching tournaments (brimstone,
sweat and napalm), I decided to implement one of my old ideas:  fix
scoring a bit so that it rewards play and not repetition.

Reading the patch closely will mostly spoil the new scoring for most,
so don't do that unless you really mean to.

This current revision does not implement feats (lists of things both
generic and role-related you can do to increase your peril and your
score.  Things like eating a cockatrice, using a =oC on the Astral
plane, stuff like that).  That's both because I haven't gotten the
whole list down pat /and/ because the additional bookeeping would
almost certainly need to change the save file format (which is not the
case with the patch as-is).

The patch adds a tally of general scoring categories that is disclosed
at game end (and with the wizardly #score command).  Scores are
considerably different (that *is* the point) so while you /can/ keep
your current record file, you probably don't want to.

Something that almost certainly will need to change:  the score is, at
one point, scaled by difficulty of the role you play.  That difficulty
is subjective and biased by my own difficulty with the various roles. 
I'd appreciate input on what is currently implemented:

Valkyries get 70% base score
Barbarians, Monks, and Samurai get 80%
Priests get 90%
Wizards get 110%
Cavemen and Knights get 120%
and Tourists get 150%

I'll follow up to this message with the patch proper.

